			<div class="content" id="post-content-2399133">
									

<p>I'm really digging the originality, and I'm <em>itching</em> to upvote, but a lot of little issues with the writing just irk me.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Things&nbsp;wot&nbsp;irk&nbsp;me...</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">hide&nbsp;silly&nbsp;irks</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The abilities are proportional to how well the instructions were followed, a subject will have greater awareness and control over their abilities the lower the error in the procedure.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Comma splice; there should be a semicolon or full stop in there.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The phenomenon is also somewhat difficult to study, as the user can no longer control follicles once they fall, or are plucked, out. In addition to being capable of undulating motions, the hair is also less receptive to static buildup.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The second sentence does not logically follow on from the first; so why do they make up an entire paragraph?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Observed behaviors also include several unconscious actions, for example, if threatened, a subject's hair may become rigid and stand on end, all over the body. Additionally, should a subject have need of an item, and reach for it, hair up the arm and on the hand will subtly point towards the desired object.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like there's at least two commas too many in there.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>D-2944-17 was capable of easily shrugging off light light blows</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm assuming the double &quot;light&quot; was just a typing error, but it stands out.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>EDIT: I noticed you haven't changed the [ACCESS DENIED] title for this on the mainlist yet! Every fine hairstyle needs a name, you know.</p>

